window.docContents[6].resolve({"/Tier-1___-statements/Theorem-files/Symbolic.Theorems.Refinement/#file-Symbolic___Theorems___Refinement":{"contents":"Paper › Symbolic/Theorems › Refinement.leanTier 1 · theorem file\n\nTier 1 · theorem file used by the symbolic proof 3 headline theorems 83 lines trust banner B1, trusted: the statement source ↗Read in full. This file states headline theorems. Proofs are cut after := and shown as ⋯; Lean checks them.This file is in the non-default library CliElfLib (its theorems need the ELF built from source).\n\n\n\nTrace Refinement for the libsignal-cli BinaryTrusted: the statement.Proves comp_refines_cli (CompRefinesCliBinary cliElfBytes, Symbolic/Specifications/Refinement/ElfBinding.lean), built by lake build CliElfLib. For the parsed AArch64 libsignal-cli ELF image (cliElfBytes, LibsignalBinary/Specifications/SignalSession/CliElf.lean) executing from plain loaded ELF memory (ElfImage.loadState, zero initial memory patches) under cliProgElf addrs, with its 18 Rust panic and 5 SampleNTT addresses resolved from .symtab (resolveCliElfAddrs), the binary refines the composed PQXDH ∘ SPQR ∘ Triple Ratchet symbolic model up to cryptographic byte collisions, and every reachable guarded CLI call either terminates with a process outcome or reaches a non-terminating SampleNTT matrix seed (CliElfProgress: no fault, trap, or unexcused divergence, DEV-CLI22; SIGABRT aborts terminate the trace at CliTraces.stop).Combined with Symbolic/Theorems/ModelSecurity.lean via comp_refinement_preservation_cli (Symbolic/Theorems/RefinementPreservation.lean), this yields signal_session_secure (Symbolic/Theorems/Security.lean). Non-vacuity of the extern and hook hypotheses (including HooksMatchPlaced at FIPS 197 aes256Enc / aes256Dec) is proved in Symbolic/Tests/ExternWitness.lean.\n\n\n\ntheorem comp_refines_cliL49–60 ↗#Trace refinement and progress for the SHA-256-pinned libsignal-cli AArch64 binary (CompRefinesCliBinary cliElfBytes, Symbolic/Specifications/Refinement/ElfBinding.lean). cliElfBytes parses as an ELF image whose 18 panic and 5 SampleNTT addresses resolve from .symtab (resolveCliElfAddrs); every reachable guarded CLI call running from plain ELF memory terminates with a process outcome except on a non-terminating SampleNTT matrix seed (CliElfProgress, DEV-CLI22); and under any valid cryptographic extern interpretation and matching CLI hooks, every guarded execution trace of cliRunElf from initDirs is explained by a reachable model run (Explains) or encounters a cryptographic collision after an explained prefix (CollisionAfterExplainedPrefix).\n\n\n\ntheorem real_prims_admissibleL64–69 ↗#The closed primitives executed by the linked ELF (realCliHooks) obey the symbolic laws: some extern interpretation satisfies ExternContractsHoldCli and agrees with realCliHooks (RealPrimsAdmissible, Symbolic/Specifications/Refinement/ElfBinding.lean).\n\ntheorem comp_refines_cli_realL71–81 ↗#Trace refinement and progress for the SHA-256-pinned libsignal-cli AArch64 binary at the real primitives (CompRefinesCliBinaryReal cliElfBytes, Symbolic/Specifications/Refinement/ElfBinding.lean): the real primitives obey the symbolic laws; cliElfBytes parses and resolves its .symtab addresses; every reachable guarded CLI call terminates except on a non-terminating SampleNTT seed (DEV-CLI22); and for every extern interpretation that satisfies the symbolic laws and agrees with realCliHooks, every guarded execution trace of cliRunElf from initDirs (no RealHooksAgreeOnInput filter) is explained by a reachable model run or encounters a cryptographic collision after an explained prefix.\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"Symbolic/Theorems/Refinement.lean","id":"/Tier-1___-statements/Theorem-files/Symbolic.Theorems.Refinement/#file-Symbolic___Theorems___Refinement"},"/Tier-2___-definitions/Computational___Specifications___/Computational.Specifications.Assumptions.KemCorrect/#file-Computational___Specifications___Assumptions___KemCorrect":{"contents":"Paper › Computational/Specifications/Assumptions › KemCorrect.leanTier 2 · definitions\n\nTier 2 · definitions used by the computational proof 2 headline theorems depend on it 64 of 119 lines trusted trust banner B2, trusted: definitions used by the statement source ↗Read the definitions shown. Only the declarations that the headline statements use are shown, with the namespace, section, open and variable commands needed to read them. The collapsed runs are theorems, which Lean checks, and definitions that no headline statement uses.\n\nδ-correctness and cryptographic well-formedness of the PQXDH primitivesTrusted: definitions used by the statement. kemHonestExchangeFails, KemDeltaCorrect, CryptoWellFormedDh, CryptoWellFormedKemδ and CryptoWellFormedPrimitivesδ are read by the δ-statement (Security/HeadlineDelta.lean under Computational/Specifications/Pqxdh/); see Computational/docs/TRUSTED_BASE.md.Kyber-1024 (libcrux_ml_kem::kyber1024 in libsignal) has a small nonzero decapsulation-failure probability (DEV-PQ21) rather than perfect KEM correctness (WellFormedPrimitives.kem_corr). Together with WellFormedPrimitivesδ (Model.lean), this file defines KemDeltaCorrect P δ, bounding the honest failure probability by δ, and CryptoWellFormedPrimitivesδ P, recording the X25519 and Kyber-1024 public-key collision bounds and wire-length rejection laws. The bound δ is taken as a hypothesis in the generic PQXDH theorems (FIPS 203, Aug. 2024, Table 1 gives δ = 2^-174.8 for ML-KEM-1024 and the Kyber v3.02 specification, §1.4, Table 1 gives 2^-174 under heuristic compression-noise models); for concrete Round-3 CRYSTALS-Kyber-1024 at realPEParams and kyber1024KemKeyGen, kyber1024_kem_delta_correct (Computational/Theorems/Lemmas.lean, statement Kyber1024KemDeltaCorrect in Computational/Specifications/LibsignalCli/Kyber1024Delta.lean) proves the rigorous bound δ = ε + 1 / 2 ^ 112 under the single CBD-noise idealization hypothesis KyberNoiseGap ε (Computational/Specifications/Assumptions/Kyber1024Correct.lean).\n\n\n\nδ-correctness of the KEM\n\ndef kemHonestExchangeFailsL48–54 ↗#Honest KEM decapsulation-failure event for key-generation seed seed and encapsulation coins r: encapsulation succeeds with some (ss, ct), yet decapsulation under the paired secret key does not return some ss (encapsulation returning none is not counted).\n\ndef KemDeltaCorrectL56–63 ↗#δ-correctness of the KEM (Fiedler–Günther, ePrint 2024/702, §2; FIPS 203 §3.3): kemHonestExchangeFails P seed r occurs with probability at most δ over uniform 64-byte seed and 32-byte r.\n\nCryptographic well-formedness\n\nstructure CryptoWellFormedDhL67–91 ↗#Cryptographic X25519 and cofactor-8 subgroup laws on P: public-key collision bound, scalar-multiplication injectivity modulo pow8, and 32-byte length of base-point subgroup preimages.\n\nstructure CryptoWellFormedKemδL93–112 ↗#Cryptographic Kyber-1024 laws on P: public-key collision bound and wire-length rejection for ciphertexts and public keys.\n\nstructure CryptoWellFormedPrimitivesδL114–117 ↗#Cryptographic well-formedness of P without perfect KEM correctness (kem_corr), combining WellFormedPrimitivesδ P, CryptoWellFormedDh P, and CryptoWellFormedKemδ P.\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"Computational/Specifications/Assumptions/KemCorrect.lean","id":"/Tier-2___-definitions/Computational___Specifications___/Computational.Specifications.Assumptions.KemCorrect/#file-Computational___Specifications___Assumptions___KemCorrect"},"/Tier-2___-definitions/Symbolic___Specifications___/Symbolic.Specifications.Refinement.Statement/#file-Symbolic___Specifications___Refinement___Statement":{"contents":"Paper › Symbolic/Specifications/Refinement › Statement.leanTier 2 · definitions\n\nTier 2 · definitions used by the symbolic proof 7 headline theorems depend on it 353 of 449 lines trusted source ↗trust banner in the header: none; the closure computes B2 for the symbolic proofRead the definitions shown. Only the declarations that the headline statements use are shown, with the namespace, section, open and variable commands needed to read them. The collapsed runs are theorems, which Lean checks, and definitions that no headline statement uses.\n\nDeclarations on this page (50)structure CliCalldef CliCall.extradef FilesVisibledef InputsForstructure CliTurndef CliTurn.initdef CliTurn.recordsdef CliTurn.opkUseddef SamePathdef scrubdef BundleFilesFlatdef HonestBundleFilesdef PreKeyNoMatchinstance instDecidablePreKeyNoMatchdef CliTurn.afterdef CliTurn.clearSessiondef BobCallAllowedabbrev BobSetupDHSecretabbrev SetupDHSecretdef KeyInDirdef LeaksFromdef runInputdef runEventOfdef coinsLendef StdinBoundeddef FilesBoundeddef ValidCallinductive CliTracesinductive CliReachabledef dhCoinSecretsdef HonestDHSecretdef InvertsGuardeddef kyberCoinEntropydef coinDrawsdef exitedZeroDrawsdef setupDHSecretsdef CoinsFreshdef RecvBodydef ReadCollisionClidef ModelAcceptsTermAfterAttackerSendsdef RepresentationsCollideOrAcceptedCollidedef SignalMsgAcceptedOnlyViaCollisiondef PreKeyStartCollidesOrRejectsdef PrefixExplainingGhostsdef NextEventCollidesdef CollisionAfterExplainedPrefixdef ExternContractsHoldClidef CompRefinesCliRdef CompRefinesClidef runFnToRelation\n\nWhole-Protocol Refinement Statement over signal-session CLI RunsDefines the signal-session CLI execution environment (CliCall, CliTurn, ValidCall, CliTraces, CliReachable), break/invert history guards (InvertsGuarded), CSPRNG coin-freshness premise (CoinsFresh), prefix-plus-collision excuse (CollisionAfterExplainedPrefix), and the generic trace-refinement statements (CompRefinesCliR, CompRefinesCli).\n\n\n\nstructure CliCallL42–48 ↗#Parameters of a single signal-session CLI invocation.\n\ndef CliCall.extraL50–51 ↗#\n\ndef FilesVisibleL53–59 ↗#Loader-admissibility and filesOf visibility for input file entries: excludes ., standard stream names, leading /, .. segments, and files exceeding Arm64.MAX_LFS_FILESIZE.\n\ndef InputsForL61–67 ↗#Process Inputs i corresponding to CLI call c over directory snapshot d.\n\nstructure CliTurnL69–75 ↗#Inter-call environment state: per-party directory snapshots, SignalMessage bodies emitted by earlier exit-0 send calls, and whether Bob is disabled (bobOff) after accepting an unmatched pre-key message alongside an existing session.\n\ndef CliTurn.initL77 ↗#\n\ndef CliTurn.recordsL79–83 ↗#Non-empty session record of p with its peer, if present.\n\ndef CliTurn.opkUsedL85–87 ↗#Whether Bob's one-time pre-key file has been emptied or removed.\n\ndef SamePathL89–90 ↗#Path equivalence up to Arm64.normalizePath.\n\ndef scrubL92–94 ↗#Remove coins and bundle/ entries (under any equivalent normalized path) after a run.\n\ndef BundleFilesFlatL96–98 ↗#Every bundle entry is a flat bundle/<name> path smaller than 2^31 bytes.\n\ndef HonestBundleFilesL100–103 ↗#Any bundle parsed from files by parseBundleFiles satisfies HonestBundle.\n\ndef PreKeyNoMatchL105–109 ↗#Bob recv of a non-whisper message while holding an existing session that is not eligible for promotion (¬ EligibleForSessionPromotion).\n\ninstance instDecidablePreKeyNoMatchL111–128 ↗#Decides PreKeyNoMatch. Correct by construction (a Decidable instance); its body need not be read.\n\ndef CliTurn.afterL130–137 ↗#Updated CliTurn after call c exits with code, out, and files.\n\ndef CliTurn.clearSessionL139–145 ↗#Delete p's session file (re-enabling Bob when p = r.bob).\n\ndef BobCallAllowedL147–148 ↗#\n\nabbrev BobSetupDHSecretL150–151 ↗#\n\nabbrev SetupDHSecretL153–154 ↗#\n\ndef KeyInDirL156–161 ↗#Secrets currently present in p's directory at turn t (long-term/prekey files and keys in p's active session record).\n\ndef LeaksFromL163–164 ↗#\n\ndef runInputL166–169 ↗#\n\ndef runEventOfL171–172 ↗#\n\ndef coinsLenL174–179 ↗#Expected coins byte length for each CLI subcommand (192 for init, 64 for send, 32 for recv).\n\ndef StdinBoundedL181–193 ↗#Size bounds on c.stdin matching the binary specifications' input domains.\n\ndef FilesBoundedL195–196 ↗#\n\ndef ValidCallL198–217 ↗#Preconditions for a guarded CLI call c at turn t: coin and file bounds, BobCallAllowed, role/session state discipline, HonestBundleFiles on init, send-counter bound < 2^32 - 1 on send, and PqFromHonest on recv.\n\ninductive CliTracesL219–241 ↗#Guarded CLI event traces generated by Rel from turn t: session deletions (clear), primitive break/invert events (breakInvert), exited CLI calls preceded by directory leaks (step), and aborted CLI calls terminating the trace (stop).\n\ninductive CliReachableL243–254 ↗#Inter-call turns reachable from t₀ via exited guarded calls and session deletions.\n\ndef dhCoinSecretsL256–262 ↗#32-byte X25519 private-key slices read from ev.coins (0..32 and 160..192 for init; 0..32 for recv; none for send).\n\ndef HonestDHSecretL264–267 ↗#Whether sk is a setup X25519 secret or a dhCoinSecrets slice of an exit-0 run in evs.\n\ndef InvertsGuardedL269–278 ↗#History guard on invertDH and invertKEM events: each follows its corresponding breakDH / breakKEM event and inverts an honest setup or coin-drawn public key.\n\ndef kyberCoinEntropyL280–283 ↗#32-byte Kyber encapsulation entropy extracted from the first byte of each 4-byte CSPRNG fill at offsets 32 + 4 * j (j < 32) of an init call's coins.\n\ndef coinDrawsL285–291 ↗#Clamped 32-byte secret draws consumed by ev (dhCoinSecrets plus kyberCoinEntropy on init; dhCoinSecrets on recv; none on send).\n\ndef exitedZeroDrawsL293–296 ↗#\n\ndef setupDHSecretsL298–301 ↗#Clamped setup X25519 secrets of r (ikA, ikB, spkB, and opkB when r.withOpk holds).\n\ndef CoinsFreshL303–309 ↗#CSPRNG coin-freshness premise for security theorems: all clamped setup X25519 secrets and clamped secret coin draws of exit-0 runs in evs are pairwise distinct (List.Nodup). Refinement theorems (CompRefinesCli*) do not assume CoinsFresh.\n\n1 declaration not shown (lines 311–313): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesDY.Libsignal.Composed.Refinement.Cli.instDecidableCoinsFresh\n\ndef RecvBodyL315–320 ↗#Inner SignalMessage body b of a received whisper or pre-key wire frame input.\n\ndef ReadCollisionCliL322–332 ↗#Whether ss already read a colliding network term on an earlier exit-0 recv event in evs.\n\ndef ModelAcceptsTermAfterAttackerSendsL334–343 ↗#Whether extending (g, ss) by attacker-known network steps and one decrypt step reading t explains evs₁ ++ [.run ev].\n\ndef RepresentationsCollideOrAcceptedCollideL345–358 ↗#Under explanation (g', ss', vis') of evs₁, either every representation of b hits RecvCollisionOn ∨ ReselectCollisionOn, or at least one representation is accepted for ev and every accepted representation hits RecvCollisionOn.\n\ndef SignalMsgAcceptedOnlyViaCollisionL360–368 ↗#SignalMessage body b in ev has a symbolic representation under (g, ss) and hits RepresentationsCollideOrAcceptedCollide under every collision-free explanation of evs₁.\n\ndef PreKeyStartCollidesOrRejectsL370–379 ↗#Pre-key message p (wire bytes b) starts a Bob session only via KyberMismatch or BobSessionStartCollidesOrImplicitRejectsOn across all collision-free explanations of evs₁.\n\ndef PrefixExplainingGhostsL381–384 ↗#Ghosts sharing g.σ that explain evs₁ via the same step sequence ss.\n\ndef NextEventCollidesL386–410 ↗#Next run event ev after explained prefix evs₁ forces a cryptographic collision on either an exit-0 recv or the plaintext of a send.\n\ndef CollisionAfterExplainedPrefixL412–420 ↗#Some prefix evs₁ of evs is explained by (g, ss, vis), and the immediately following run event forces NextEventCollides.\n\ndef ExternContractsHoldCliL422–426 ↗#Machine-independent external crypto contracts: ExternCryptoLawsHold, canonical X25519 public keys, and rejection of X25519 torsion shifts.\n\ndef CompRefinesCliRL428–440 ↗#Whole-protocol CLI trace refinement starting from initial directory family dirs: for every valid interp, agreeing W, and well-formed r, there exist opaque semantics S such that every guarded trace evs is either explained (Explains) or hits CollisionAfterExplainedPrefix.\n\ndef CompRefinesCliL442–445 ↗#Whole-protocol CLI trace refinement starting from initDirs.\n\ndef runFnToRelationL447 ↗#\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"Symbolic/Specifications/Refinement/Statement.lean","id":"/Tier-2___-definitions/Symbolic___Specifications___/Symbolic.Specifications.Refinement.Statement/#file-Symbolic___Specifications___Refinement___Statement"}});